        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "lock_acquire_attempts",
            "type": "int32",
            "description": "lock_acquire_attempts bounds how many times a cycle retries a contended\n per-user lock before giving the record back to the queue.\n\n kernel.FencedLock.Acquire is NON-BLOCKING — a key held by a different\n holder returns granted=false rather than parking the call — so a contended\n acquire is a poll, and something has to bound the polling. Giving up is not\n a failure: the record has not been ACKed, so it is redelivered, and by then\n the instance that held the lock has finished the cycle that would have\n absorbed it anyway.\n\n Config rather than a constant for the same reason messaging's\n max_recipients is: contention is a property of the deployment, and changing\n it must not need a redeploy.",
