            "name": "retrieved_grace_seconds",
            "type": "int32",
            "description": "retrieved_grace_seconds is how long after retrieval a row stays\n NEVER-evict before the sweep marks it WINDOW.\n\n Zero — the default — is the decision doc's ruling taken literally:\n \"retrieved_at_ms is the point item 4's eviction eligibility starts counting\n from\". Marking at grace 0 makes the row's `(spec.store_epoch)`, which is\n what the residency window is measured against, equal to the retrieval\n instant, so the window counts from retrieval and from nothing else.\n\n It is a knob rather than a constant because a client that acks and then\n immediately re-reads is a real pattern, and a non-zero grace keeps the row\n resident across that gap. It can never make an UNRETRIEVED row evictable:\n the sweep's predicate is status == RETRIEVED before it is anything else.",
