  "description": "Identity holds the public verifying keys for kernel's token exchange service.\n Kernel is the sole token authority — all tokens (S2S, U2S, refresh) and\n X.509 certificates are signed by kernel's keys.\n\n Token exchange handles:\n   1. Direct exchange: delegate presents cred_pair JWT or cloud proof → token/cert\n   2. Delegation: broker (oauth, K8S) authenticates via header, mints on behalf\n\n Access: RW for kernel, RO for every service that declares a\n (spec.state_imports) of kernel.Identity. Enforced at run time by the\n generated SecurityAuthenticator.checkAccess on every state RPC — services\n that only need to verify tokens read the public JWKS view instead.",
  "fields": [
    {
