      "message": {
        "name": "Grant",
        "package": "kernel",
        "description": "Grant is a standing delegation: a user authorizes a delegate (an intermediary\n service, e.g. an agent acting on a schedule) to act on their behalf later,\n asynchronously. Kernel\n stores the GRANT, never a minted token — the delegate holds only `id`.\n\n On use the delegate presents its own S2S identity plus `id`; kernel replays\n `claims` into OPA fresh (the same EntitlementEvalInput shape\n `IdentityServiceImpl.buildClaimsStruct` already builds from a token payload),\n intersects the result with `authorized_scope`, and mints a short-lived token\n (sub=subject, act=delegate_name, azp=kernel — kernel mints Grant tokens\n directly, so azp is always the closed-enum `kernel` value; the delegate name\n goes on the `act` claim instead). Fresh OPA gives \"cannot exceed the user's\n current authority\"; the recorded scope gives \"the user downscoped it\". Nothing\n is snapshotted that can go stale except the claims themselves — which catches\n policy changes, never IDP changes.\n\n This message is carried in KernelDiskState and mutated at runtime by\n Mint.RevokeGrant (revoked_at_ms) only; there is no create/list RPC yet — the\n catalog is still seeded from Config.grants at boot.\n\n PROVISIONAL: this field set is a prerequisite storage layer built ahead of,\n not instead of, the design conversation with the maintainer. What is settled:\n id, delegate_name, subject, authorized_scope, claims, created_at_ms,\n expires_at_ms, revoked_at_ms. NOT settled: how the system learns a user's IDP\n claims changed or the user was deleted — claim-provenance and epoch are still\n open and may add fields here.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "id is the opaque grant identifier the delegate holds and presents. Unique\n across the cluster.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "default_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 32768,
                "defaulted": true,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "default_bound"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "delegate_name",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "delegate_name is the Delegate.name of the intermediary holding this grant.\n It becomes the minted token's act claim (azp on a Grant mint is always\n kernel — see the message comment above).",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 512 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 512,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "subject",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "subject is the user this grant acts for — the sub of the token that will be\n minted, and the identity whose claims were recorded below.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 512 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 512,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "authorized_scope",
            "type": "message (recursive reference: entitlements.TokenEntitlements)",
            "description": "authorized_scope is the per-service scope the user recorded at consent time.\n Every mint intersects the fresh OPA result with this, so the grant can only\n ever narrow the user's live authority, never widen it."
          },
          {
            "name": "claims",
            "type": "message",
            "description": "claims are the user's IDP claims as captured at consent time, in the same\n google.protobuf.Struct shape that userentitlements.EntitlementEvalInput.claims\n takes, so they can be replayed into OPA verbatim."
          },
          {
            "name": "created_at_ms",
            "type": "int64",
            "description": "created_at_ms is the consent time, epoch milliseconds.",
            "constraints": [
              "must be \u003e= 0"
