{
  "name": "Config",
  "package": "scotty",
  "description": "Config is delivered by kernel at startup and on every change.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "max_open_tickets",
      "type": "int32",
      "description": "max_open_tickets bounds how many tickets may be open at once, and exists\n for the same reason tasks.Config.max_open_tasks does: to give the service a\n rule that comes from CONFIG rather than from code, so changing it in kernel\n changes behaviour with no redeploy.\n\n NOT a written policy. §2 is explicit that \"an entitlement makes an action\n impossible, a written policy makes it inadvisable\" — a config bound that\n hard-fails a create is neither, it is a resource limit on the service. No\n business rule may be expressed here.",
      "default": 1000
    },
    {
      "name": "max_chain_hops",
      "type": "int32",
      "description": "max_chain_hops is the CIRCUIT BREAKER on AI-mediated negotiation, and it is\n a HOP COUNT, not a duration. A chain's hop count is the number of turns\n taken in it — every Ticket, TicketAdvice and TicketComment sharing a\n chain_id — and when it reaches this bound Scotty stops adding its own\n judgement to that chain. Jody, 2026-08-30: \"it escalates to the human at\n the same level. It just keeps LLMs from getting stuck in a loop.\"\n\n Config for the same reason max_open_tickets is: it is a resource-shaped\n bound on the service, changeable in kernel with no redeploy, and it is NOT\n a written policy — nothing here decides anything about a request.\n\n A wall-clock TTL was proposed for this and explicitly discarded; see\n loopers/schematic/decisions/ticket-ttl-hop-count-circuit-breaker-2026-08-30.md.",
      "default": 20
    },
    {
      "name": "llm_credential",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "llm_credential is the Anthropic API key, fanned out by operator into this\n service's generated bootstrap config under the YAML key \"llm_credential\"\n (see platform/proto/services/operator.proto's Config.llm_credential and\n .llm_credential_services, and operator.yaml's own llm_credential_services\n list, which must include \"scotty\" for the fan-out to reach here). Field\n name and type must match what operator's bootstrap.go writes, or the\n service fails to unmarshal its own generated config.",
