            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
          {
            "name": "request_id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "request_id is the JOIN KEY to the accounting plane — the same value\n accountingrecord.AccountingRecord carries under the same name with the same\n EQ query_field, so \"which accounting rows belong to the request that wrote\n this row\" and \"which row did that request write\" are one predicate asked of\n two record types. Without it provenance stops at the accounting plane's\n edge, which is precisely where §4's auditor starts.\n\n Empty is legitimate, not an error: an unauthenticated path has no Caller to\n read one from, so a required-and-absent field would fail the publish rather\n than record the gap.",
