{
  "name": "ScottyActivity",
  "package": "scotty",
  "description": "ScottyActivity is the ARTIFACT left by every write into knowledge.\n\n §1: \"Nothing reaches knowledge without leaving an artifact. Authored facts —\n a phone number, a written policy, a stated deadline — are not distilled from\n anything, so if current state could change with no immutable record, the\n authored half is unrecoverable.\" ScottyState's requires_artifact_on_write\n enforces that this type exists; this is that type.\n\n §4 is the reason it is a generated RECORD rather than something the service\n writes for itself: \"Scotty must not be the writer of the accounting. If it\n were, 'doesn't rat Dennis out' becomes 'can omit'... Accounting is a\n byproduct of the call path, stamped at the generated seam.\" The neutral\n auditor reads THIS, and this carries what was DONE — entity kind, entity id,\n principal, request id — never what was said.\n\n spec.record implies spec.event, so tacplus synthesizes the topic wrapper\n ScottyActivityBus with topic ref scotty.ScottyActivityBus.stream. Do NOT\n hand-write that wrapper.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "activity_id",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "activity_id is the record key: one row per WRITE, not one per entity.",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 160 bytes",
        "minimum size: 1"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 160,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_min_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 1,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "entity_kind",
      "type": "enum",
      "description": "entity_kind and entity_id name what was written. EQ-filterable, because\n \"every artifact for this ticket\" is the question provenance has to answer.",
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_enum_defined",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "enum_values": [
        {
          "name": "SCOTTY_ENTITY_KIND_HUMAN",
          "number": 1
        },
        {
          "name": "SCOTTY_ENTITY_KIND_POLICY_VERSION",
          "number": 2
        },
        {
          "name": "SCOTTY_ENTITY_KIND_TICKET",
          "number": 3
        },
        {
          "name": "SCOTTY_ENTITY_KIND_TICKET_ADVICE",
          "number": 4
        },
        {
          "name": "SCOTTY_ENTITY_KIND_TICKET_DECISION",
          "number": 5
        },
        {
          "name": "SCOTTY_ENTITY_KIND_TICKET_COMMENT",
          "number": 6
        },
        {
          "name": "SCOTTY_ENTITY_KIND_TICKET_CHAIN",
          "number": 7,
          "description": "A TICKET_CHAIN artifact is left ONCE per chain, on the hop that reaches\n Config.max_chain_hops — the moment Scotty stops mediating. entity_id is the\n chain_id. It records that AI mediation hit its limit, which is a thing that\n was DONE and therefore belongs in the auditor's store; no ticket is decided\n by it."
        }
      ],
      "filter_mode": "eq"
    },
    {
      "name": "entity_id",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 128 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 128,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "filter_mode": "eq"
    },
    {
      "name": "occurred_at_ms",
      "type": "int64",
      "description": "occurred_at_ms is the RANGE criterion — \"what happened between D1 and D2\"\n is the auditor's own question.",
      "filter_mode": "range"
    },
    {
      "name": "acted_by",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "acted_by is the principal on whose behalf the write happened. NOT redacted:\n §4 says a finding is a citation naming \"action A by principal X at T\", and\n a citation whose principal egress clears is not a citation.\n It is also the ROW'S OWNING PRINCIPAL for the record query plane's c2s\n half. spiffe_id below is the record's declared owner but is the PUBLISHER\n — eventbus stamps scotty's own service identity onto it — so filtering a\n user's reads on that field would show every user nothing. acted_by is the\n authenticated human the write happened for, taken from the verified token\n (service.rs `principal()`) or from the written row's own (spec.principal)\n field, never from anything the caller writes. That is the value the\n generated wrapper's row filter must compare against.\n The EQ criterion is what carries the row filter into the plane's SIZE-ONLY\n RPCs: Get\u003cT\u003eCount returns a number over the handle's predicate and no rows,\n so no egress filter can narrow it. The generated c2s wrapper pins this\n criterion to the caller at Create\u003cT\u003eQuery, and every later call on the\n handle inherits it.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 256 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 256,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "filter_mode": "eq"
    },
    {
      "name": "spiffe_id",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "spiffe_id is the record owner. The name is LOAD-BEARING: eventbus's topic\n discovery matches the literal field name \"spiffe_id\" of string type when it\n decides which topics get publisher-identity stamping, so renaming this\n field silently turns the stamping off.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 1024 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 1024,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "filter_mode": "eq"
    },
    {
      "name": "request_id",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "request_id is the JOIN KEY to the accounting plane — the same value\n accountingrecord.AccountingRecord carries under the same name with the same\n EQ query_field, so \"which accounting rows belong to the request that wrote\n this row\" and \"which row did that request write\" are one predicate asked of\n two record types. Without it provenance stops at the accounting plane's\n edge, which is precisely where §4's auditor starts.\n\n Empty is legitimate, not an error: an unauthenticated path has no Caller to\n read one from, so a required-and-absent field would fail the publish rather\n than record the gap.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 128 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 128,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "filter_mode": "eq"
    },
    {
      "name": "spiffe_actor",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "spiffe_actor is the DELEGATE that made the call, stamped by EventBus from\n the token's `act` claim at publish time — the agent acting for the person\n in acted_by, unset in the ordinary non-delegated case. Provenance only: it\n is never the principal, and sys/spec.proto forbids wiring it into one.\n\n The service does not set it and must not: like spiffe_id above, a value\n written here would be a claim about identity that nothing verified.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 1024 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 1024,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "namespace",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "namespace is the row's owning TENANT: the namespace claim of the caller\n whose write this artifact records. It is the tenant half of the identity\n acted_by carries the subject half of — that field's (spec.store_principal)\n answers \"are these MY rows\", this one answers \"is this MY tenant\", by EXACT\n string equality against the caller's claim (never the level-or-below\n containment the administrative namespace rule uses).\n\n MANDATORY, not opt-in: tacplus (ValidateRecordNamespaceAnnotations) fails\n generation for any (spec.record) declaring no such field, on the reasoning\n that the record nobody remembered to annotate is exactly the one that leaks.\n\n The filter is generated on the READ side, which is not this record's own\n s2s publish surface above: stratum's record query plane (the (spec.trait) in\n vservices/query.proto) exposes a c2s List/Sample/Watch over EVERY record in\n the fleet, and the namespace check is spliced into each of them for this\n type. A row reaching one of those with a namespace other than the caller's\n halts the JVM rather than failing the one call.\n\n Bounded like acted_by.\n\n AN EQ (spec.query_field), and it did not used to be. The reasoning that kept\n it off was that a boundary is not a caller-supplied predicate — which is\n right about the CALLER and wrong about the SERVER. The client-facing read\n plane pins this field to the caller's verified namespace claim BEFORE the\n store is asked, and a pin needs a criterion to be pinned into; the record\n store evaluates only the criteria a record annotates, so without this line\n the pin is generated and silently ignored, leaving the aborting egress\n filter as the only tenant boundary. tacplus refuses (spec.record).c2s_read\n on a record whose namespace field is not EQ-queryable, for exactly that\n reason.\n\n It stays uncallable by clients, which is the part the old comment cared\n about: the emitted GetScottyActivityRequest and ListScottyActivityRequest\n carry no namespace field, and ScottyActivityReadFilter — the only filter a\n c2s caller supplies — is generated without one.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 256 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 256,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ],
      "filter_mode": "eq"
    },
    {
      "name": "trace_id",
      "type": "string",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 32768 bytes (default)"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "default_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 32768,
          "defaulted": true,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "default_bound"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "noop",
      "type": "bool"
    }
  ]
}

