{
  "name": "Ticket",
  "package": "scotty",
  "description": "Ticket is the IMMUTABLE CORE of a request. §3: \"The ticket is a general\n primitive, not a time-off feature — request, routed, advised, decided,\n commented, immutable, appendable, accounted. It covers overrides, permits and\n approvals generally, and it exercises the entire stack.\"\n\n NO STATUS FIELD, and that is not an omission. \"Immutable\" and \"a lifecycle\n enum this row keeps up to date\" are contradictory, and the lifecycle is\n already fully derivable: a ticket is decided iff a TicketDecision exists for\n it, advised iff a TicketAdvice does. Storing it twice creates a state that\n can disagree with the records it summarises. See the schematic looper's\n decisions/ticket-status-derived-not-stored.md (pre-split snoopy history,\n not in this repo).\n\n NO KIND/CATEGORY FIELD either. §5: \"Prose earns fields once the pattern is\n known; a field never degrades to prose because it got inconvenient.\"\n Time-off, override and permit tickets have not yet shown a common structure,\n so classifying them now would be inventing the taxonomy. request_text carries\n it as attributed prose until the pattern is known. See the schematic\n looper's decisions/ticket-kind-field-deliberately-absent.md (pre-split\n snoopy history, not in this repo).\n\n NO (spec.store_principal), unlike tasks.Task. That option filters reads to\n the row's creating caller, which would make a routed ticket unreadable BY THE\n PERSON IT IS ROUTED TO — the one read the primitive exists to serve.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "ticket_id",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 64 bytes",
        "minimum size: 1"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "bool",
          "bool_value": true,
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 64,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        },
        {
          "rule": "assert_min_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 1,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "requested_by",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "requested_by is the authenticated PRINCIPAL that opened the ticket, stamped\n from the token by the generated wrapper (see CreateTicketRequest). It is\n the token subject, not a Human id, because it has to be the thing the\n platform can actually vouch for.",
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 256 bytes"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_max_size",
          "target": "field",
          "value_kind": "int",
          "int_value": 256,
          "unit": "bytes",
          "source": "annotation"
