{
  "name": "TicketAdvice",
  "package": "scotty",
  "description": "TicketAdvice is Scotty's advice, SEALED.\n\n §3: \"The advice is sealed when given, not composed at decision time.\n Otherwise a Scotty built to serve Dennis softens a warning it knows he's\n about to override — nobody would have to instruct it to.\" And: \"Immutable to\n Dennis_Scotty too, not only to Dennis.\"\n\n Sealing here is STRUCTURAL, not a flag. There is no UpdateTicketAdvice RPC in\n the Scotty service, so no caller — human or agent — has a mutation path to\n reach. A `sealed: bool` would be decoration; an absent RPC is not.\n\n Advice may be given more than once on a ticket (\"Ruiz is back Friday\"). Each\n giving is a new sealed row, and the LAST one is the final advice. The design\n record says the ticket carries \"the final advice PLUS the asserted facts that\n moved it, not the deliberation\" — the append chain is that, with the\n intermediate rows retained rather than discarded. See\n decisions/ticket-advice-append-vs-single-row.md.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "advice_id",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "constraints": [
        "maximum size: 128 bytes",
        "minimum size: 1"
      ],
      "constraint_infos": [
        {
          "rule": "assert_required",
