      "description": "user is whose agent ran, and the ROW'S OWNING PRINCIPAL.\n\n (spec.store_principal) is what holds a caller's reads of this record to\n their own rows on the c2s query plane, and it is the reason the Bird's Eye\n View needs no filtering code: \"my cycles\" is the only query the plane will\n answer. `spiffe_id` below is the record's declared owner but holds THIS\n SERVICE's identity (eventbus stamps the publisher), so filtering on that\n would show every user nothing.\n\n The EQ criterion is what carries the filter into the plane's size-only\n RPCs, which return a number over the handle's predicate and no rows for an\n egress filter to narrow.",
