            "type": "message",
            "description": "human_viewed is the separately-typed human signal. Unset at publish, and\n unset for as long as the person has not looked, which is the normal state\n of a delivered message.",
            "message": {
              "name": "HumanViewedReceipt",
              "package": "messaging",
              "description": "HumanViewedReceipt fires when the actual person looked at the message. A\n distinct signal from AgentReceivedReceipt above: an agent can have ACKed a\n message hours before a human sees it, and business-hours-deferred\n presentation makes that gap the normal case rather than the exception.\n\n Presentation is a passive pull label — the reader is told \"viewed\", never\n pushed a notification. That is the design already built for tickets\n (decisions/ticket-read-receipts-2026-08-30.md), relocated to where it\n belongs.",
              "fields": [
