          {
            "name": "namespace",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "namespace is the row's owning TENANT, by EXACT string equality against the\n caller's namespace claim (never the level-or-below containment the\n administrative namespace rule uses). It is the tenant half of the identity\n `recipient` carries the subject half of: that field's (spec.store_principal)\n answers \"are these MY rows\", this one answers \"is this MY tenant\".\n\n MANDATORY, not opt-in: tacplus (ValidateRecordNamespaceAnnotations) fails\n generation for any (spec.record) declaring no such field, on the reasoning\n that the record nobody remembered to annotate is exactly the one that leaks.\n\n TWO DIFFERENT ENFORCEMENTS, and they are not the same failure:\n   - WRITE (this record's publish path). eventbus's PublishHandler stamps\n     this field from the publishing token's namespace claim and REFUSES the\n     publish with PERMISSION_DENIED when the token carries none. Stamp-or-\n     refuse, deliberately not stamp-if-empty: a row published with an empty\n     namespace is a row no legitimate caller can ever read.\n   - READ (stratum's record query plane, c2s half). The generated egress\n     filter holds every row to the reader's own claim, and a row that fails\n     the comparison HALTS THE JVM rather than failing the one call — the\n     filter is the backstop behind the store's own query, so it firing means\n     that query is broken.\n\n Bounded like every other string here. Not a (spec.query_field): the field\n exists to be the egress boundary, and making it a caller-supplied predicate\n is not what a boundary is.",
            "constraints": [
