          {
            "name": "ejectionable",
            "type": "enum",
            "description": "ejectionable is item 4's marker and this record's whole reason to exist —\n the first per-row use of it in the fleet.\n\n The values are not decoration and are not derivable from `status` by the\n store: the store does not know what HELD means, and UNSPECIFIED is defined\n as never-evict precisely so a marker an author forgets keeps the row.\n\n   HELD      -\u003e EJECTIONABLE_NEVER   (explicitly, not left at UNSPECIFIED:\n                the row is stating a policy, not omitting one)\n   RETRIEVED -\u003e EJECTIONABLE_WINDOW  (set by UpdateHeldMail inline, or by\n                the sweep when a grace period deferred it)\n\n WHAT \"EVICT\" DOES, stated plainly because the decision doc left it open:\n it evicts the row FROM MEMORY. It does not delete it. `Residency`'s own\n definition — \"a warm row evicted from memory is still complete and\n queryable on disk\" — is the semantics, and deletion is retention's job\n above, ninety days from arrival. There is deliberately no EVICTED status\n and no delete path here: a status this service wrote would be a claim about\n the store's memory that this service cannot observe.",
            "enum_values": [
              {
