      ],
      "message": {
        "name": "AccountingRecord",
        "package": "accountingrecord",
        "description": "AccountingRecord is one completed RPC, stored in full by stratum.\n\n Every service in the fleet is a producer, so the s2s surface is open to all\n service identities. There is no c2s surface: accounting rows are written by\n the chassis, never by a browser client.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "accounting_id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "accounting_id is the record key: one row per accounting event.",
            "required": true,
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 128 bytes",
              "minimum size: 1"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_required",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 128,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              },
              {
                "rule": "assert_min_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "request_id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "request_id is THE correlation key — the x-request-id the gateway generates\n and every hop forwards. The EQ query_field is what lets a caller ask \"which\n accounting rows belong to the request that wrote this row\", which is the\n whole reason this record exists rather than a log line.",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 128 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 128,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
          {
            "name": "source_id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "source_id identifies the emitting process (\"{service_id}-{instance_id}\"),\n copied verbatim from accounting.Event.source_id.",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 256 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 256,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
          {
            "name": "timestamp_ms",
            "type": "int64",
            "description": "timestamp_ms is the RANGE criterion — \"everything in this window\".",
            "filter_mode": "range"
          },
          {
            "name": "level",
            "type": "enum",
            "description": "level is carried on the envelope so a consumer can filter without\n inspecting the payload; same reasoning applies to the stored row.",
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_enum_defined",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "bool",
                "bool_value": true,
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "enum_values": [
              {
                "name": "EVENT_LEVEL_DEBUG",
                "number": 1
              },
              {
                "name": "EVENT_LEVEL_INFO",
                "number": 2
              },
              {
                "name": "EVENT_LEVEL_WARN",
                "number": 3
              },
              {
                "name": "EVENT_LEVEL_ERROR",
                "number": 4
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "method",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "method is the RPC that was accounted for.",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 256 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 256,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
          {
            "name": "code",
            "type": "int32",
            "description": "code is the gRPC status code the call completed with."
          },
          {
            "name": "duration_ms",
            "type": "int64",
            "description": "duration_ms is the measured call duration."
          },
          {
            "name": "principal_sub",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "principal_sub is the verified human principal behind the call — the claim\n the Authorizer actually checked, not a caller-written header. Caller-decided\n redaction, the same leg TaskActivity.created_by exercises: redacted by\n default, raw only for a caller holding a matching data grant.\n It is also the ROW'S OWNING PRINCIPAL for the record query plane's c2s half:\n (spec.store_principal) is what the generated wrapper filters a user's reads\n down to, and it must name the HUMAN, not spiffe_id below. spiffe_id is the\n emitting service, so filtering on it would narrow every user to the rows it\n emitted itself — which for a human is none. The two annotations disagree on\n purpose and this one wins, exactly as sys/spec.proto describes.\n\n The row filter runs BEFORE the redaction above, on the raw stored value, so\n a caller without the data grant is still matched against its own principal\n rather than against a redacted string.\n NOT a (spec.query_field), deliberately, and that is a real tension rather\n than an oversight. Making it an EQ criterion is what would carry the row\n filter into the plane's SIZE-ONLY RPCs — Get\u003cT\u003eCount returns a number over\n the handle's predicate and no rows, so no egress filter can narrow it — but\n ValidateDataEntitlementAnnotations refuses a field that is both\n (spec.redact) and (spec.query_field), because a filterable field defeats\n redaction. That refusal is right for the S2S half of the plane, where no\n per-caller pin applies and a peer could filter on this field freely.\n\n So accounting ROWS are filtered to the caller at egress and accounting\n COUNTS are not. Closing that needs a per-surface criterion (c2s-only,\n wrapper-pinned) which does not exist today; it is written up in the item 2\n report rather than bought by weakening the redaction rule.",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 256 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 256,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "data_entitlement_mode": "may_redact"
          },
          {
            "name": "spiffe_id",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "spiffe_id is the record owner: the EMITTING SERVICE's identity, not the end\n user's (the human principal is principal_sub above). The field name is\n load-bearing — eventbus's topic discovery matches the LITERAL name\n \"spiffe_id\" of string type to decide which topics get publisher-identity\n stamping, so renaming it silently turns the stamping off.",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 1024 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1024,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
          {
            "name": "store_epoch_ms",
            "type": "int64",
            "description": "store_epoch_ms is this row's LAST-WRITE clock, Unix milliseconds, owned and\n stamped by the generated wrapper — a producer that supplies one is refused\n (INVALID_ARGUMENT), so the value can never be caller-influenced.\n\n It is what makes RESIDENCY_WARM above possible: the residency window is\n measured from this clock, and it is the predicate the memory and disk legs\n partition the query on. RESIDENCY_WARM without it fails generation\n (ValidateResidencyAnnotations VAL-3) rather than silently tiering on the\n wrong clock.\n\n NOT timestamp_ms: that is the emitting service's business clock, the one\n retention above measures age from. Two different clocks; only this one is\n store-owned. On an append-only record they are written together and never\n diverge afterwards — which is a property of THIS record, not of the epoch.",
            "filter_mode": "range"
          },
          {
            "name": "namespace",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "namespace is the row's owning TENANT: the namespace claim of the caller\n whose RPC this row accounts for. (spec.store_namespace) is the tenant twin\n of principal_sub's (spec.store_principal) above — the same egress seam, a\n different boundary. That one answers \"are these MY rows\"; this one answers\n \"is this MY tenant\", by EXACT string equality against the caller's claim.\n\n MANDATORY, not opt-in: tacplus (ValidateRecordNamespaceAnnotations) fails\n generation for any (spec.record) declaring no such field, on the reasoning\n that the record nobody remembered to annotate is exactly the one that leaks.\n\n The filter is generated on the READ side, which is not this record's own\n s2s publish surface above: stratum's record query plane (the (spec.trait) in\n the app proto's vservices/query.proto) exposes a c2s List/Sample/Watch over\n EVERY record in the fleet, and the namespace check is spliced into each of\n them for this type. A row reaching one of those with a namespace other than\n the caller's halts the JVM rather than failing the one call.\n\n Bounded like every other string field on this message. Not a\n (spec.query_field): the field exists to be the egress boundary, and making\n it a caller-supplied predicate is not what a boundary is.",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 256 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 256,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "principal_sub_redacted",
            "type": "bool",
            "description": "tacplus data-entitlement: per-field redacted indicators. Set true by\n the generated sanitize transform when the paired field is redacted;\n lets a consumer distinguish a redacted value from a genuine empty one."
          },
