                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
          {
            "name": "spiffe_actor",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "spiffe_actor is the DELEGATE that made the call, stamped by EventBus from\n the token's `act` claim at publish time — the agent acting for the person\n in acted_by, unset in the ordinary non-delegated case. Provenance only: it\n is never the principal, and sys/spec.proto forbids wiring it into one.\n\n The service does not set it and must not: like spiffe_id above, a value\n written here would be a claim about identity that nothing verified.",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 1024 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 1024,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "name": "namespace",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "namespace is the row's owning TENANT: the namespace claim of the caller\n whose write this artifact records. It is the tenant half of the identity\n acted_by carries the subject half of — that field's (spec.store_principal)\n answers \"are these MY rows\", this one answers \"is this MY tenant\", by EXACT\n string equality against the caller's claim (never the level-or-below\n containment the administrative namespace rule uses).\n\n MANDATORY, not opt-in: tacplus (ValidateRecordNamespaceAnnotations) fails\n generation for any (spec.record) declaring no such field, on the reasoning\n that the record nobody remembered to annotate is exactly the one that leaks.\n\n The filter is generated on the READ side, which is not this record's own\n s2s publish surface above: stratum's record query plane (the (spec.trait) in\n vservices/query.proto) exposes a c2s List/Sample/Watch over EVERY record in\n the fleet, and the namespace check is spliced into each of them for this\n type. A row reaching one of those with a namespace other than the caller's\n halts the JVM rather than failing the one call.\n\n Bounded like acted_by.\n\n AN EQ (spec.query_field), and it did not used to be. The reasoning that kept\n it off was that a boundary is not a caller-supplied predicate — which is\n right about the CALLER and wrong about the SERVER. The client-facing read\n plane pins this field to the caller's verified namespace claim BEFORE the\n store is asked, and a pin needs a criterion to be pinned into; the record\n store evaluates only the criteria a record annotates, so without this line\n the pin is generated and silently ignored, leaving the aborting egress\n filter as the only tenant boundary. tacplus refuses (spec.record).c2s_read\n on a record whose namespace field is not EQ-queryable, for exactly that\n reason.\n\n It stays uncallable by clients, which is the part the old comment cared\n about: the emitted GetScottyActivityRequest and ListScottyActivityRequest\n carry no namespace field, and ScottyActivityReadFilter — the only filter a\n c2s caller supplies — is generated without one.",
            "constraints": [
              "maximum size: 256 bytes"
            ],
            "constraint_infos": [
              {
                "rule": "assert_max_size",
                "target": "field",
                "value_kind": "int",
                "int_value": 256,
                "unit": "bytes",
                "source": "annotation"
              }
            ],
            "filter_mode": "eq"
          },
