types.description:
TimeseriesFieldOption configures how a single proto field maps to a timeseries
 column. Applied via (spec.timeseries_column) on individual fields. Any field
 with this annotation becomes a column; fields without it are omitted. Column
 roles are store-neutral: order_key/partition_key name logical roles and
 cardinality_hint states distinct-value intent — a downstream materializer maps
 them onto the concrete engine's sort/partition/encoding mechanisms.

 Example:
   string session_id = 1 [(spec.timeseries_column) = {order_key: 1}];
   int64 timestamp_ms = 2 [(spec.timeseries_column) = {order_key: 2, partition_key: true}];
   string event_type = 3 [(spec.timeseries_column) = {cardinality_hint: CARDINALITY_LOW}];
   int64 duration_ms = 4 [(spec.timeseries_column) = {}];

types.schema_json:
{
  "name": "TimeseriesFieldOption",
  "package": "spec",
  "description": "TimeseriesFieldOption configures how a single proto field maps to a timeseries\n column. Applied via (spec.timeseries_column) on individual fields. Any field\n with this annotation becomes a column; fields without it are omitted. Column\n roles are store-neutral: order_key/partition_key name logical roles and\n cardinality_hint states distinct-value intent — a downstream materializer maps\n them onto the concrete engine's sort/partition/encoding mechanisms.\n\n Example:\n   string session_id = 1 [(spec.timeseries_column) = {order_key: 1}];\n   int64 timestamp_ms = 2 [(spec.timeseries_column) = {order_key: 2, partition_key: true}];\n   string event_type = 3 [(spec.timeseries_column) = {cardinality_hint: CARDINALITY_LOW}];\n   int64 duration_ms = 4 [(spec.timeseries_column) = {}];",
