            "description": "delivery_id is the record key: \"\u003cmessage_id\u003e/\u003crecipient\u003e\". One per\n (message, recipient) pair, which is what makes the N publishes of one\n submission N separately-keyed records rather than N copies of one.\n\n Derived rather than random ON PURPOSE: the value a caller would need to\n reconstruct to ACK a delivery is exactly (which message, for whom), so\n deriving it means an agent that knows both never has to have been told the\n id. It is also what makes the fan-out replay-safe — a retried submission\n regenerates the same delivery ids rather than a second set of rows.",
